# Mirrors .gitignore, plus dev-only files the image never needs.
#
# THE PATTERNS ARE NOT .gitignore PATTERNS, and one of them was silently
# doing nothing because of it (#1358). Docker matches each line against the
# whole context-relative path rather than against every path segment, so a
# bare `__pycache__/` excludes only `backend/__pycache__` and lets
# `app/core/__pycache__` straight through. `COPY app/ ./app/` and
# `COPY alembic/ ./alembic/` are recursive, so that is not hypothetical:
# measured 2026-09-09, a local build shipped 81 `.pyc` files in 8
# directories into the image - bytecode compiled on whoever ran the build,
# inside the artifact that gets deployed. A clean CI checkout has no
# `__pycache__` to copy, which is exactly why this went unseen.
#
# The rest genuinely is belt-and-suspenders against a future broader COPY:
# `.venv/`, the cache directories and `tests/` only ever exist at the top
# level, where a bare pattern does match. `**/` is used only where nesting
# is real, rather than sprayed everywhere to look thorough.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
*.duckdb
.env
tests/
.git/
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
README.md
